helo:8000005 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        helo:0000003 ;
    rdfs:label "thesaurus"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "The learning topic of thesauri, controlled vocabularies arranged in a known order whose equivalence, hierarchical and associative relationships between terms (use and used for, broader and narrower, related) are shown by standard relationship indicators used in both directions, such as a vocabulary recording QALY as an equivalent of quality-adjusted life year."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "NISO 2005, sections 4 and 8" ;
    dcterms:source "Baines D. Scope of the learning pathways ontology, 18 October 2026, passed on by Michelle Ashley in the HELO 0.2.0 brief, building block 4 of 6 of the semantic layer" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    helo:9000023 helo:8000004 .

helo:8000006 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        helo:0000003 ;
    rdfs:label "ontology"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "The learning topic of ontologies, explicit specifications of a conceptualisation, which in the healtheconomics.wiki family state either the concepts of health economics and their relationships, as HEO does, or, in the realist sense, the kinds of real things those concepts are about, as RHEO does, with tasks, outcomes, values and mathematics alongside."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Gruber 1993; RHEO 0.4.0 README" ;
    dcterms:source "Baines D. Scope of the learning pathways ontology, 18 October 2026, passed on by Michelle Ashley in the HELO 0.2.0 brief, building block 5 of 6 of the semantic layer" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> .

helo:8000007 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        helo:0000003 ;
    rdfs:label "knowledge graph"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "The learning topic of knowledge graphs, graphs of data intended to gather and convey knowledge of the real world, whose nodes stand for things of interest and whose edges stand for relationships between them, such as the HEO and RHEO graph together. The definition is an inclusive one and is contested."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Hogan et al. 2021" ;
    dcterms:source "Baines D. Scope of the learning pathways ontology, 18 October 2026, passed on by Michelle Ashley in the HELO 0.2.0 brief, building block 6 of 6 of the semantic layer" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> .

