    owl:annotatedTarget heto:4000013 ;
    heao:9000001 heao:4000002 ;
    helo:9000009 1.00 ;
    helo:9000010 "4 of the 4 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Conduct sensitivity analysis are core concepts of Building the Model (Parameter Uncertainty, Scenario Analysis, Sensitivity Analysis, Structural Uncertainty), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. HETO's own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly."@en ;
    helo:9000021 4 ;
    helo:9000022 4 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000428 ;
    owl:annotatedProperty helo:9000007 ;
    owl:annotatedSource helo:5000002 ;
    owl:annotatedTarget helo:4000004 ;
    helo:9000010 "Review B of HELO 0.2.0 (19 October 2026) proposes that Measuring Health Gain is primarily for the outcomes researcher, for Darrin Baines to confirm. The site does not state who the pathway is for."@en ;
    helo:9000020 "primarily" .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    rdfs:comment "The outline row of module 9 names all six ontologies in its interactive piece and real material, so the module's material uses the Health Economics Axiology Ontology (HEAO). Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. A module whose material uses an ontology records that use and does not describe the ontology."@en ;
